※ pl4g-test: compile=ok run=native,qemu exit=23 diag=none

※ The label is what makes a jump able to mean a loop other than the one it
※ stands in.  All four jumps a pair of loops has are written here: the inner
※ loop's own next turn, the inner loop left, and the outer loop left from
※ inside the inner one -- the last of which no unlabelled jump could say.
※
※ Two loops that are not one inside the other may share a label, there being no
※ place both could be named from; one inside the other may not, since the inner
※ would hide the outer and leave no way to name it.
※
※ A name a jump hands over is the name as it stands where the jump is: `found`
※ is assigned in the inner body, so both loops carry it, and what follows them
※ reads what the way out of them left.

@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    let found: mut u8 = 0u8
    foreach §rows r := 0u8…4u8:
        foreach §cols c := 0u8…4u8:
            if c = 0u8:
                ※ the inner loop's own next turn
                continue §cols
            if r × c = 6u8:
                found ← r × 10u8 + c
                ※ leaves both loops at once
                break §rows
            if c > r:
                ※ leaves the inner loop only, and the outer one carries on
                break §cols
    found
